[h1]Big Copilot: the business dashboard Big Ambitions never gave you.[/h1]
Ten shops, two warehouses, a factory and forty employees. Which business is losing money? Which shelf runs empty tomorrow? Who is about to quit? The game knows, but the answers are spread over a hundred screens. [url=https://bigcopilot.com]Big Copilot[/url] puts them on one board.

[b]Free, runs in your browser, no account.[/b]

[h2]What the board shows you[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Today:[/b] only what needs you now. Stock about to run out, staff whose demands are not met, a shop turning customers away at its ceiling, a factory standing idle.
[*][b]Every business ranked by profit,[/b] with its own page: trends, costs, customers by hour, the crew and when it pays back what you put in.
[*][b]Supply:[/b] what each shop really uses, every delivery plan and import contract in one place, what to import each week, and a seven-day wholesale shopping list.
[*][b]Staffing:[/b] a week of hours for each business, nobody over the 12-hour limit, every station covered, and how many people to hire.
[*][b]Growing:[/b] demand for every business type in every neighbourhood, a location finder that ranks every free building, and plans for a new store, a factory or a headquarters: what it costs and, for a store, when it breaks even.
[*][b]Real estate:[/b] every building you own with its occupancy, income and best rent, and buildings for sale ranked by payback.
[*][b]A city map and a wiki:[/b] your businesses on the map, the game's help pages, and a setup guide for every kind of shop.
[/list]

[h2]What this mod adds[/h2]
Without the mod, Big Copilot reads a save file you pick. With it, the board reads the game you are playing, keeps up as you play, and can make changes in your game for you.

[list]
[*][b]A live board:[/b] while a city is loaded, the mod hands the running game to Big Copilot in your browser, on your own PC. It refreshes every game hour, after every game save, and when you click Update. You no longer pick a save folder or look for the newest Recover save.
[*][b]Staff a business in one step:[/b] spare staff move to the businesses that need them first, only the rest are hired from the headhunters' candidates, and every week involved is written at once. Candidates are only picked into weeks that fit their demands: hours, days, free weekends, no mornings or evenings.
[*][b]Weekly schedules:[/b] write a business's staffing plan into the game.
[*][b]Uniforms:[/b] set the default uniform wherever a role has none.
[*][b]Imports:[/b] apply the planned amounts to your purchasing agents' import contracts.
[*][b]Marketing:[/b] switch on the cheapest mix of campaigns that brings a business to full promotion, through the agencies already in your phone's contacts.
[*][b]Rent:[/b] set the best rent on the buildings you own, through the game's own seven-day wait.
[*][b]Wholesale orders:[/b] place a weekly delivery or a one-off order for a shop with a wholesaler in your contacts. Deliveries follow the game's normal Monday 08:00 schedule; nothing is rushed and nothing is charged up front.
[/list]

[h2]Every change is checked first[/h2]
[list]
[*]The board shows what the game will do before you apply it.
[*]The mod checks each change against the rules the game's own screens enforce. If one part is refused, nothing is written.
[*]If the game has changed since the board last read it, the change is refused and nothing is written.
[*]Undo takes the last change of each kind back; staffing, rent and wholesale changes on the same game day. Hired candidates return to the candidate list (they are not fired), and moved staff go back with their old hours.
[*]The first change from a browser asks for your approval in the game. After that the browser is remembered.
[/list]

[h2]How to use it[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, then enable [b]Big Copilot Link[/b] in the game's Mods menu.
[*]Load a save.
[*]Open [url=https://bigcopilot.com]bigcopilot.com[/url] and click [b]Link to the game[/b]. Chrome and Edge ask once whether the site may connect to devices on your local network. That device is the mod on your own PC, so allow it.
[/olist]

[h2]Your data stays on your PC[/h2]
[list]
[*]The mod listens on 127.0.0.1:8322 only. Nothing outside your PC can reach it.
[*]It answers bigcopilot.com and pages on your own PC. Other websites get nothing.
[*]The board reads your company in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.
[*]The only thing the mod stores is the list of browsers you approved. It changes your game only when you apply a change on the board from an approved browser.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]A save made with any mod enabled is a modded save. If you load an unmodded save with the mod on, the game asks "Load with mods?" and writes a copy named "(Modded)", leaving your original save as it was. The game turns bug reporting off for modded saves. That is the game's rule for every mod.
[*]The mod does nothing while the board is closed. It only refreshes when Big Copilot has asked in the last two minutes.
[*]Options, under Big Copilot Link in the game's mod options: switch it off, change the port (8322 to 8325), refresh every game hour, refresh when a building loads, forget approved browsers.
[*]Made for game build 3682, on Windows and macOS. What changed in each version is under Change Notes.
[/list]

